The out-of-domain probe confirmed the compiler warning concretely: an unsupported `#bin("-"…)` reaches a residual term and the LLVM interpreter exits 113. A Boolean-list probe is not terminating promptly under the proof backend, so I’m treating it only as an excluded-domain diagnostic and will bound/stop it rather than misclassify it as a candidate failure.
